From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] deko3d: invariant gl_Position in every vertex shader

The Xbox 360 computes the same position bit for bit wherever the same code computes it, and games rely on it: a
depth prepass, then a base pass testing GEQUAL against it. Each variant of a vertex shader (its kept outputs) was
compiled on its own and uam fused and reordered the position math differently in each, so Deadpool's base pass,
drawn with another variant of the same vertex shader than its prepass, failed the depth test everywhere (the world
black). SpirvAGlsl now declares `invariant gl_Position;` in every vertex shader.

---
diff --git a/src/ui/deko3d/glsl.cpp b/src/ui/deko3d/glsl.cpp
--- a/src/ui/deko3d/glsl.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/deko3d/glsl.cpp
@@ -283,6 +283,16 @@
     }
 
     r.glsl = compilador.compile();
+    // Every vertex shader's position invariant: the Xbox 360 gives the same position bit for bit wherever the same
+    // code computes it, and games rely on it (a depth prepass, then the base pass testing GEQUAL against it). Here
+    // each variant of a vertex shader (its kept outputs, `salidas`) is compiled on its own, and uam fused and
+    // reordered the position math differently in each: Deadpool's base pass, with another variant of the same vertex
+    // shader than its prepass, failed the depth test everywhere (the world black). GLSL's `invariant` makes Mesa
+    // compute it exactly as written in every variant.
+    if (r.vertices) {
+      const size_t fin_version = r.glsl.find('\n');
+      if (fin_version != std::string::npos) r.glsl.insert(fin_version + 1, "invariant gl_Position;\n");
+    }
     if (quitar && !QuitarSalidas(r.glsl, quitar, r.error)) {
       r.glsl.clear();
       return r;
-- 
